   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public health law, in relation to requiring the\ncommissioner of health to consult with the office of addiction services and\nsupports to publish certain guidance on maternal depression screenings, and to\namend a chapter of the laws of 2024 amending the public health law relating to\nmaternal depression screenings, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S.\n2039-B and A. 2870-B, in relation to the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S802",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S802-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2500-k, Pub Health L; amd §3, Chap of 2024 (as proposed in S.2039-B & A.2870-B)",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S802\n\nSPONSOR: BROUK\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public health law, in relation to requiring the\ncommissioner of health to consult with the office of addiction services\nand supports to publish certain guidance on maternal depression screen-\nings, and to amend a chapter of the laws of 2024 amending the public\nhealth law relating to maternal depression screenings, as proposed in\nlegislative bills numbers S. 2039-B and A. 2870-B, in relation to the\neffectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to L.2024, c.644, which\ndirects the Department of Health (DOH) to create standards for incorpo-\nrating maternal depression screenings into routine perinatal care.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill amends the underlying chapter by requiring the Commissioner of\nHealth to consult with the Office of Addiction Services and Supports in\naddition to the Office of Mental Health and other stakeholders in iden-\ntifying and publishing existing guidance for providers on incorporating\nmaternal depression screenings into routine care. The chapter amendment\nalso makes technical changes to the underlying bill and extends the\neffective date to 18 months after the bill becomes law.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 644 of the Laws of 2024. S.2039-B and\nA.2870-B both passed the Senate and Assembly during the 2023 Legislative\nSession.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately; provided, however, that section\none of this act shall take effect on the same date and in the same\nmanner as a chapter of the laws of 2024 amending the Public Health Law\nrelating to maternal depression screenings, as proposed in legislative\nbills numbers S.2039-B and A. 2870-B, takes effect.\n",
